.TH PLUGIN-QUALIFICATION-DB 1 2026-11-19 plugin-db-qualification "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plugin-qualification-db \- query the OpenMixer qualification store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plugin-qualification-db query
.RB [ \-\-sha256
.IR hash ]
.RB [ \-\-format
.IR format ]
.RB [ \-\-uri
.IR uri ]
.RB [ \-\-offer
.IR offer ]
.RB [ \-\-host\-class
.IR class ]
.RB [ \-\-rate
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-quantum
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-pkg\-format
.IR f ]
.RB [ \-\-pkg\-name
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-pkg\-version
.IR v ]
.RB [ \-\-pkg\-release
.IR r ]
.RB [ \-\-pkg\-distro
.IR d ]
.RB [ \-\-pkg\-arch
.IR a ]
.RB [ \-\-binary\-path
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-layer
.IR user | base ]
.RB [ \-\-records ]
.B \-\-json
.RI [ common\ options ]
.br
.B plugin-qualification-db counts
.RB [ \-\-layer
.IR user | base ]
.B \-\-json
.RI [ common\ options ]
.br
.B plugin-qualification-db check
.RI [ common\ options ]
.PP
.IR "common options" :
.RB [ \-\-base
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-user
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-contract\-dir
.IR dir ]
or
.BR \-\-scope " " user | system
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the qualification store with libplugin-qualification-db: the base database installed by
plugin-qualification-records and the user layer, merged by whole record (a user record shadows every base
record of its plugin, offer and host class). The command is the reader for programs that cannot link the library.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B query \-\-json
Prints one JSON object per line for every result the filters match, user layer first. The keys, in this order:
.BR layer ,
.BR sha256 ,
.BR format ,
.BR uri ,
.BR offer ,
.BR host_class ,
.BR set ,
.BR pkg_format ,
.BR pkg_name ,
.BR pkg_version ,
.BR pkg_release ,
.BR pkg_distro ,
.BR pkg_arch ,
.B binary_path
(the main binary's path below its install root),
.BR layout_scheme ,
.BR layout_sha256 ,
.B tested_version
(strings, null when the record holds none),
.B unpinnable
(0 or 1),
.B files
(the record's per-file list in its order: an array of objects with
.B path
and
.BR sha256 ,
never empty), the cell's
.BR rate ,
.B quantum
and
.BR outcome ,
the cost, latency and memory figures with their has_ flags, and
.B verdicts
(every verdict of the record). Words and numbers only.
.TP
.B query \-\-json \-\-records
Prints one JSON object per line for every RECORD the filters match (the results of one record are one line):
.BR layer ,
.BR sha256 ,
.BR format ,
.BR uri ,
.BR offer ,
.BR host_class ,
.B set
(the record's set, null for a user-layer record) and
.BR record ,
the whole record as a document of plugin-qualify.qualification-record/1. The same filters apply. With
.B \-\-rate
and
.BR \-\-quantum ,
given together (one alone is refused, exit 2), the records printed are the ones that claim that cell, one for each
plugin key: the reference tier's record first, and within a tier the set measured later, as the claim table of the
base says. A key nobody holds at that cell prints no line.
.TP
.B counts \-\-json
Prints one JSON object per line for every format, in format order:
.BR format ,
.B plugins
(the plugins of that format, a plugin being a format and a uri),
.B offered
(those with a record that has a tier_offered row) and
.BR not_offered .
The merged answer, or one layer with
.BR \-\-layer .
.TP
.B check
Opens both layers, checks every word column against the installed contract domains, and checks the key rule for
every record of both layers: the key's SHA-256 is the SHA-256 of the entry of the record's list whose path is its
binary_path. Prints
.B ok
and exits 0, or prints the refusal code and its message and exits 1; a record that breaks the key rule gives
.BR qualification-db.key-mismatch ,
naming the key and the path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-base " path"
The base database. Default: the value of
.BR PLUGIN_QUALIFICATION_DB_BASE ,
else /usr/share/omx/qualification/qualification.sqlite.
.TP
.BI \-\-user " path"
The user layer; an empty path reads none. Default: the value of
.BR PLUGIN_QUALIFICATION_DB_USER ,
else the layer under the home directory of the effective user,
.IR ~/.local/share/omx/qualification/qualification.sqlite .
An absent user layer is an empty layer.
.TP
.BI \-\-contract\-dir " dir"
The contract directory the word check reads. Default: the value of
.BR OMX_CONTRACT_PATH ,
else the installed contract directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-scope " user|system"
Opens the production places of that scope as the library does (the installed base, and the user layer under the home
of the effective user, or the system layer under /var/lib/omx/qualification), whatever the environment says. The
default, with none of the options above, is the user scope's places, with the variables below. It is a usage error
(exit 2) with
.BR \-\-base ,
.B \-\-user
or
.BR \-\-contract\-dir .
.TP
.BI \-\-binary\-path " path"
(query) Only records whose main binary's path is exactly
.IR path ,
as stored: relative to the install root, case-sensitive, no suffix match.
.TP
.BI \-\-layer " user|base"
(query, counts) Only that layer's records: the user layer's every record of the filters, none shadowed, or the base's,
including a record the user layer shadows. Without it, the merged answer.
.SH ABSENT BASE
A base file that does not exist is an empty base layer, not a refusal: the answer is the user layer's alone and the exit
status 0. The command says so on standard error, never on standard output, which holds records only: one line,
.BR "plugin-qualification-db: base-absent: <path>: the base layer is empty" ,
is written by
.B query \-\-json
and
.BR "counts \-\-json" ,
and
.B check
prints
.BR "ok base-absent" .
A present base writes no such line.
Only a missing file is absent; a base that exists and cannot be used (a directory, no read permission, not a SQLite
database, another schema version) is refused by name.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR PLUGIN_QUALIFICATION_DB_BASE ,
.BR PLUGIN_QUALIFICATION_DB_USER
and
.BR OMX_CONTRACT_PATH
are read by this command only, and a flag beats its variable. The library reads no environment variable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when the store is refused (the code is
.B qualification-db.unreadable ,
.BR qualification-db.not-a-store ,
.BR qualification-db.schema-mismatch ,
.BR qualification-db.schema-other ,
.BR qualification-db.domain-too-old ,
.BR qualification-db.word-unknown ,
.BR qualification-db.hot-journal ,
.BR qualification-db.busy ,
.B qualification-db.layer-unknown
(a library caller named another layer), for
.B check
.B qualification-db.key-mismatch ,
or a code of the contract loader); 2 on a usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/omx/qualification/qualification.sqlite
The base database.
.TP
.I /usr/share/plugin-qualification-db/qualification.sql
The DDL of the store (the schema variable of plugin-qualification-db.pc).
